From 11afefb736432bb9b7dcdf8a26c1b21a2e0f66d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spindle rig <spindle@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 06:22:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Serve MatrixRTC transports (MSC4143) and delayed events
 (MSC4140)

A call client checks unstable_features for both before it will place a
call, and a mesh node served neither: a client that trusted the 200 from
a plain send removed itself from the call at once, and Element Call did
not schedule the departure at all and left the ghost.

- GET /_matrix/client/v1/rtc/transports (and the MSC4143 unstable path)
  answers the LiveKit JWT services named in NEUTRINO_RTC_LIVEKIT_URL,
  comma separated; empty is a working configuration
- org.matrix.msc4140.delay on /send and /state holds the event, with
  list, send, cancel and restart under the MSC4140 unstable prefix;
  restart re-applies the whole original delay, which is what makes it a
  heartbeat; the send is authorised by the room actor when it fires, not
  when it is scheduled; a day is the longest delay and a thousand the
  most one user may hold
- both advertised on /versions

Delays are kept in memory: a restart drops them, and rtc.rs says why
that is the accepted trade on a phone and what the next step is.
